[h1]Having a problem? Post it here[/h1]

[i]In other languages:[/i] [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/german/reporting-a-problem.md]Deutsch[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/spanish/reporting-a-problem.md]Español (España)[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/latam/reporting-a-problem.md]Español (Latinoamérica)[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/french/reporting-a-problem.md]Français[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/italian/reporting-a-problem.md]Italiano[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/polish/reporting-a-problem.md]Polski[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/brazilian/reporting-a-problem.md]Português (Brasil)[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/turkish/reporting-a-problem.md]Türkçe[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/russian/reporting-a-problem.md]Русский[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/thai/reporting-a-problem.md]ไทย[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/japanese/reporting-a-problem.md]日本語[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/schinese/reporting-a-problem.md]简体中文[/url] · [url=https://github.com/tfoxy/sts2-couch-coop/blob/main/workshop/discussions/koreana/reporting-a-problem.md]한국어[/url]

Post here if something goes wrong: a crash, a player who can't finish joining, something drawn wrong, a run that breaks.

[b]If your phone or tablet can't open the join page at all[/b], read [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussion/3799476240/563668239243032720/]Can't connect from a phone?[/url] first. Most connection problems are a Wi-Fi, firewall or router setting covered there.

[h3]Before you report a stuck join[/h3]
Starting a player's game can take up to a minute, especially on a slower computer. While the line under [b]Joining…[/b] on the join page keeps counting up and changing, it is still working, so keep the page open.

[hr][/hr]
[h1]What to include[/h1]

You don't need to answer everything. The first two help the most.

[h3]1. What happened, and what you expected[/h3]
A sentence or two is enough. If an error appeared, copy it exactly, including the smaller grey line under it, or post a screenshot or a photo of the screen.

[h3]2. The connection report (joining or lobby problems)[/h3]
[i]Skip this if the problem happened during a run.[/i]

On the computer, open [b]Couch Co-Op QR Code[/b], then look under [b]Connections[/b]. Select the failed connection under [b]Connection problems[/b], choose [b]Copy report[/b], and paste it into your post.

It says which step failed and how long each step took, includes what the host thinks went wrong, and lists the paths to the log files below.

[h3]3. The log files[/h3]
If you copied the connection report, it already lists the exact paths.

[b]The game log[/b], on the host computer:
[list]
[*]Windows: [i]%APPDATA%\SlayTheSpire2\logs\godot.log[/i]
[*]Linux: [i]~/.local/share/SlayTheSpire2/logs/godot.log[/i]
[*]macOS: [i]~/Library/Application Support/SlayTheSpire2/logs/godot.log[/i]
[/list]

[b]Player logs.[/b] Each player who joins runs their own hidden copy of the game on the host computer, with its own log. If a player got stuck joining, their log usually explains why; the game log usually doesn't.

The first player to join is slot-2, the next slot-3, and so on. For slot-2:
[list]
[*]Windows: [i]%APPDATA%\SlayTheSpire2\couch-coop\headless-slots\slot-2\SlayTheSpire2\logs\godot.log[/i]
[*]Linux: [i]~/.local/share/SlayTheSpire2/couch-coop/headless-slots/slot-2/SlayTheSpire2/logs/godot.log[/i]
[*]macOS: [i]~/Library/Application Support/SlayTheSpire2/couch-coop/headless-slots/slot-2/Library/Application Support/SlayTheSpire2/logs/godot.log[/i]
[/list]

If there is no [i]headless-slots[/i] folder, the log is [i]couch-coop/seat-logs/slot-2.log[/i], inside the same [i]SlayTheSpire2[/i] folder as the game log.

[b]Which lines matter.[/b] In both logs, the lines I need most are the ones containing [i][couchcoop][/i] (for example [i][INFO] [couchcoop] ...[/i]), plus any [i][ERROR][/i] line, even one that doesn't mention couchcoop. Those are usually enough.

[b]Before you paste a whole log:[/b] this board is public. A log contains your SteamID64 (a long number starting with 7656 that links to your Steam profile) and your computer's user name in file paths. It doesn't contain passwords or other players' accounts. If you'd rather not share those two, replace them before pasting, or post only the [i][couchcoop][/i] and [i][ERROR][/i] lines and I'll ask if I need more.

[h3]4. Versions and mods[/h3]
[list]
[*]Whether you are on the [b]stable[/b] or [b]public beta[/b] branch of the game.
[*][b]Other mods you have installed.[/b] Every player's copy of the game loads the same mods as the host, so another mod can stop a player from joining even when the host's game works fine.
[*]The host's operating system.
[*]Your CouchCoop version, if you know it. Otherwise I'll assume the latest.
[/list]

[h3]5. Anything that narrows it down[/h3]
[list]
[*]Does it happen every time, or only sometimes?
[*]Does it happen for every player, or just one?
[*]Did it work before, and did anything change since, like a game update or a new mod?
[/list]
